<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <!--
      PREVIEW MODE (scaffolded by framework-go-app-generator/webgen). This page boots the SAME
      <App/> as index.html over the fixture transport (src/previewShell/main.tsx).
      Its own CSP is the preview's full response CSP less frame-ancestors (which a
      <meta> cannot carry), so the page fetches nothing from another origin whatever
      server hosts it: no request, image, script, style, font, prefetch, worker or
      frame. framework-web's previewFixtures build plugin fails a build whose CSP
      differs from PREVIEW_META_CSP.
      A CSP does not govern navigation. A same-tab link, location.href or a meta
      refresh to another origin is refused and reported by framework-web's
      navigation guard where the browser has the Navigation API (Chromium today),
      and only reported, or not caught at all, elsewhere. The preview origin holds
      no cookies and no secrets, so what such a navigation can carry out is the
      fixture data; that residual is accepted.
      Built by vite.preview.config.ts into dist-preview/index.html.
    -->
    <meta
      http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
      content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'"
    />
    <title>@@APP@@ · preview</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/previewShell/main.tsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>
